questions.questionText:
In a circle with center O, chords AB and CD intersect at right angles at point X inside the circle.
(a) If angle XAD = 35°, find:
(i) angle ADX;
(ii) angle BCD;
(iii) angle BOD.
State clearly the geometric reason for each step.

(a) State what is meant by work function energy of a metal surface.
(b) Light of wavelength 380 nm is incident on a sodium surface having work function 2.28 eV. Calculate:
(i) the photon energy in electron-volts;
(ii) the maximum kinetic energy of emitted photoelectrons in Joules;
(iii) the de Broglie wavelength of an electron having this maximum kinetic energy.

(a) State three reasons why the 1992 Constitution provides for the Separation of Powers.
(b) State two functions of each of the following arms of government in Ghana:
(i) The Executive;
(ii) The Legislature;
(iii) The Judiciary.
